1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,885
A language model can recommend a trade in seconds.

2
00:00:02,885 --> 00:00:05,193
The hard part is trusting it with money.

3
00:00:05,193 --> 00:00:11,135
AlphaAgent puts three models in an argument, then hands the answer to code that cannot be talked round.

4
00:00:11,135 --> 00:00:16,270
No prompt can move money here; only the guard, which knows nothing about language models.

5
00:00:16,270 --> 00:00:17,670
Here is the interface.

6
00:00:17,670 --> 00:00:23,334
A request to buy forty-five shares of NVDA at a hundred dollars arrives at the portfolio.

7
00:00:23,334 --> 00:00:29,888
The guard approves ten point four nine units instead - one thousand forty-nine dollars, eighteen cents.

8
00:00:29,888 --> 00:00:31,225
Five percent of cash.

9
00:00:31,225 --> 00:00:37,970
Every limit is visible in the same header: exposure, concentration, per-trade size and the daily loss cap.

10
00:00:37,970 --> 00:00:39,446
Three agents argued first.

11
00:00:39,446 --> 00:00:41,547
A bull analyst built the case to buy.

12
00:00:41,547 --> 00:00:45,805
A risk assessor built the case to sell, and neither saw the other's prompt.

13
00:00:45,805 --> 00:00:50,688
The chief investment officer weighed both and named the objection it could not answer.

14
00:00:50,688 --> 00:00:53,640
Nothing about their disagreement is summarised away.

15
00:00:53,640 --> 00:00:56,735
The deliberation is on screen, not summarised away.

16
00:00:56,735 --> 00:01:02,439
Claims, evidence and the rebuttal that answered them, each tagged with its source and horizon.

17
00:01:02,439 --> 00:01:07,900
Positive coverage on the left, negative on the right, and the decision quality underneath.

18
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:11,903
And every request is checked against limits the model cannot see.

19
00:01:11,903 --> 00:01:18,124
A second request after a six hundred dollar loss is refused, because the daily limit is five hundred.

20
00:01:18,124 --> 00:01:20,957
The arithmetic is printed next to the refusal.

21
00:01:20,957 --> 00:01:24,960
The refusal names the rule, the amount and the limit it breached.

22
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:32,622
Run the decision again and you get the same answer, from a replay bundle you can open in a browser with no database and no key.

23
00:01:32,622 --> 00:01:34,010
Open source, on GitHub.
